The key takeaway:

> **Rate limiting doesn't just protect your API. It protects everything behind your API.**

Choosing the right algorithm depends on your requirements:

⚡ **Fixed Window** → Simple
🎯 **Sliding Window** → More accurate
🪣 **Token Bucket** → Controlled bursts
💧 **Leaky Bucket** → Smooth traffic
🌐 **Redis + Distributed Rate Limiting** → Multiple service instances

Building reliable distributed systems isn't just about handling more traffic.

It's about **controlling traffic intelligently.**

